<<<
blunder, &

1351

+ easily shown to be absurd. Had she, had I, are the inverted equivalents of if she had, if I had; no-one would defend if she had have done, nor if I had have been, & it follows that Had she done, Had I been, are the only correct inverted conditionals.
===
blunder, &

+ easily shown to be absurd. *Had she*, *had I*, are the inverted equivalents of *if she had*, *if I had*; no-one would defend *if she had have done*, nor *if I had have been*, & it follows that *Had she done*, *Had I been*, are the only correct inverted conditionals.
>>>

